Semicolons inside single-quoted literals and SQL comments are content in a
SQL data source, and a column named like a SQL builtin (`FORMAT`) does not
disturb classification (feature.diagnostics_pipeline A19). The near miss
for datasource_sql_semicolon: nothing here is a bare separator.
-- input.ds --
/* conversions: 'all;pdf' and 'doc;txt'; keep in sync */
update report_profile
set FORMAT = 'all;pdf' -- previous value was 'doc;txt'; see ticket
where profile_id = 7
